[b]Bestiary Lens[/b]

A contextual bestiary card for Queen's Domain. Aim at an enemy to see its unlocked bestiary information in a compact, native-style card using the game's own localized text, fonts, panels and item icons.

[b]Displayed information[/b]
[list]
[*]Base HP, attack and XP
[*]Slash, pierce and impact resistance
[*]Standard loot entries, item icons, base drop rates and coin quantities when available
[/list]

Undiscovered and excluded enemies reveal no name, stats or loot. The mod reads save progression but does not write save data or alter combat, loot or progression.

[b]Controls[/b]
[list]
[*]F9: show or hide the card
[*]F10: open the displayed enemy's unlocked bestiary entry, including controller focus
[/list]

[b]Requirements[/b]
[list]
[*]Queen's Domain, Windows game build (UE 4.27.2)
[*]UE4SS with Lua support and LoopInGameThreadWithDelay
[/list]

UE4SS, the game and game assets are not included. Install and configure UE4SS separately. The mod references assets already present in the game.

[b]Limitations[/b]
[list]
[*]Stats and drop percentages are base values; luck, pity and game-specific overrides can change actual results.
[*]The adapter reads two standard drop slots. Custom drop logic or unsupported schemas may produce incomplete or unknown loot information.
[*]Targeting uses visible mesh bounds and an obstruction trace, not triangle-perfect hit detection.
[*]Missing native captions are omitted; the mod does not add translations.
[*]Compatibility with other UE4SS builds, long-session stability and all third-party mod combinations are not exhaustively tested.
[/list]
